    },
    {
      "id": "quote:f0a191d76d140c07",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 244,
        "char_start": 201,
        "episode_id": "1c0614c2-9f65-5fd5-9340-ab8c6059d014",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "Thanks, A. correspondent. Great to be back.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 12000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 6000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p08_e03.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "person:speaker-01",
      "properties": {
        "name": "A. correspondent"
      },
      "type": "Person"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:e163c71c1a70969e",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 409,
        "char_start": 263,
        "episode_id": "1c0614c2-9f65-5fd5-9340-ab8c6059d014",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Today's episode is sponsored by Squarespace. Squarespace makes building a beautiful, branded website actually pleasant. Try squarespace.com today.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 18000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 12000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p08_e03.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:743c6436bb89ef63",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 511,
        "char_start": 409,
        "episode_id": "1c0614c2-9f65-5fd5-9340-ab8c6059d014",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "What does the failure mode look like? What's the structural angle most listeners don't have access to?",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 24000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 18000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p08_e03.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:6e2159612a72541b",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 713,
        "char_start": 533,
        "episode_id": "1c0614c2-9f65-5fd5-9340-ab8c6059d014",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "Yeah, so \u2014 A newsroom is a reliability system with a deadline. We've seen this play out at teams using BBC. The framing matters because it tells you which trade-offs you're making.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 30000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 24000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p08_e03.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:d9ee007eb2b376f0",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 803,
        "char_start": 732,
        "episode_id": "1c0614c2-9f65-5fd5-9340-ab8c6059d014",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Walk me through a concrete example. How does BBC fit into this picture?",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 36000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 30000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p08_e03.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:51787e75cd8126b1",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 985,
        "char_start": 825,
        "episode_id": "1c0614c2-9f65-5fd5-9340-ab8c6059d014",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "Here's how I think about it. Trust is the only asset a public broadcaster actually owns. If you ignore that, you end up rebuilding it from scratch a year later.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 42000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 36000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p08_e03.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    }
  ],
